Vim text editor

Install:
  Install missing Vim and create a configuration with line numbers when ~/.vimrc is absent.

Upgrade:
  Update installed Vim and append the line-number setting to an existing configuration when the setting is absent.

Status:
  Report the installed package version and whether ~/.vimrc contains the line-number setting.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  Configuration file: ~/.vimrc
  Managed setting: set number
  Install preserves existing configuration; upgrade preserves existing lines and does not create an absent configuration file.
